    "recommendations": "• Install a reflective address marker at the driveway entrance so responders can confirm the correct property from the road.\n• Mark the driveway entrance with reflective posts on both sides to help responders locate the turn-in at night or in reduced visibility.\n• Keep the full length of the driveway clear of parked vehicles so emergency apparatus can reach the residence without stopping.\n• Maintain enough vertical clearance along the driveway for a fire engine or ambulance to pass without obstruction from overhanging branches.\n• Identify a designated turnaround area near the residence and keep it clear at all times so apparatus is not required to back out the full length of the driveway.\n• Post the property address visibly at both the road entrance and again near the main residence to help responders confirm their location after traveling the access drive.\n• Keep a clear path between the main residence and the detached structure so responders can move between buildings without navigating around obstacles.\n• Trim dense vegetation along the sides of the driveway to maintain a clear line of sight for drivers and to allow two vehicles to pass or a single apparatus to maneuver.\n• Identify and communicate the single access point limitation to your local fire station so they are aware before an incident occurs.\n• Keep the vehicle parking area clear of stored equipment or materials that would reduce the available space for staging a responding unit."
  },
