    "recommendations": "• Remove woody debris piles visible near the structure.\n• Thin scattered shrubs around the perimeter of the structure to increase open space between plants and the building.\n• Cut back ground vegetation growing directly against the foundation and walls.\n• Trim any shrubs or low branches along the driveway to keep the travel path clear for vehicles.\n• Remove dead or dry material from brush areas closest to the structure.\n• Keep shrubs in the brush areas nearest the house separated from each other so fire cannot easily move between plants toward the structure.\n• Clear woody debris from the area surrounding any outbuildings or secondary structures on the property.\n• Maintain the long driveway free of overhanging branches and encroaching shrubs along its full length to allow emergency vehicle access.\n• Remove accumulated dead leaves, sticks, and plant debris from the ground around the base of the structure.\n• Keep the area immediately around the house clear of stacked wood, debris, or dried plant material."
